  // The terrains of the map: the RELIEF of a hex (what lies under the vegetation), the water and
  // the wetlands.
  //
  // Every passable land relief has a "family" — plain, hill or mountain — and the climate turns it
  // into one of its VARIANTS: the same plain is a tundra plain at the poles, a boreal plain in the
  // cold belt, a steppe or a prairie in the mild one, a savanna in the subtropical one and a
  // tropical plain near the equator (see data/climate.json). The variant is the terrain of the hex:
  // it is what the game stores and what the resources are placed on. There is no generic "plain" on
  // the map — a plain is always one of its varieties.
  //
  // The NAME of a variety is the climate zone and the relief together: "Tundra, Plain",
  // "Boreal, Plain", "Tropical, Hills". The mountains are the same in every zone, so their name
  // carries no zone — they are just "Mountains". The cover of a hex is appended to the name when
  // the hex is shown to the player: "Tropical, Hills, tropical forest"
  // (GameData.terrain_display_name).
  //
  // The family is what the game means by "a plain" wherever the climate does not matter:
  // a resource that grows on allowed_terrain ["plain"] grows on all six of them, and the
  // vegetation of a hex is taken from the cover_chance of its climate zone (data/climate.json),
  // not from the terrain record.
  //
  // The variants of one family share the icons of the family: nothing in the drawing tells the
  // varieties of one relief apart yet — the climate is read from the name of the terrain in the
  // tooltip, not from its colour. "color" is the flat colour of the hex, used where no icon is
  // available.
  //
  // The WETLAND family "swamp" is built the same way: the Voronoi spreads the family and the
  // climate turns every hex of it into the bog of its belt. The varieties of the swamp are fewer
  // than the zones — only the belts whose wetlands really differ from their neighbours get a record
  // of their own — and all of them are named "Swamps", the way every mountain is "Mountains".
  "terrains": [
    // --- THE POLAR BELT: the tundra -------------------------------------------------------
    // The coldest belt, the closest to the poles: the same relief as everywhere else, only the
    // ground is bare — nothing but moss and lichen grows on it (data/climate.json).
